      "body": "When in-process restart is enabled, a failure in `destroy_global_state()` or `GlobalState.reset_for_restart()` is logged and swallowed by Bridge's cleanup callback. NVRx's `ThreadedFinalize` does not forward worker exceptions, so finalization appears successful despite incomplete cleanup.\n\nRecord the cleanup error and relay it on the caller thread after the worker joins. This preserves successful cleanup and lets NVRx abort the retry on a finalization failure. Tests use native NVRx composition/threaded finalization with mocked CUDA access and cleanup endpoints.\n\nRelated upstream glue: NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#7029. Bridge owns its separate restart wrapper; no MCore patch or paired PR is needed. This applies to the documented in-process path with an NVRx release that includes the deprecated API.\n\nValidation (2026-10-22):\n- Unmodified Bridge base: `ec062aa39f2b7817b0e0f93f4283dcbe514eddfa`.\n- Execution MCore pin: `89b28875a8d786ab41333bc60e7e8022e83e8f65`; upstream comparison base: `4b9d4f1459ad1c4fc59e405f23861c0ed0836769`.\n- Identical red/green command: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_inprocess_restart.py -k test_finalize_propagates_cleanup_errors -q -p no:cacheprovider`.\n- Before production edits: exit 1, four failures (`DID NOT RAISE RuntimeError`) and two passing success controls. After: exit 0, six passed. Both cleanup failure sites and cache settings are covered; successful subsequent cleanup does not replay the error.\n- Adjacent: `uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_inprocess_restart.py tests/unit_tests/training/test_state.py -k 'inprocess_restart or reset_for_restart' -q -p no:cacheprovider` — exit 0, 31 passed.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` — passed, no file modifications.\n- CPU callback-contract validation; no complete GPU fault-recovery result is claimed. Sequential read-only review found no blocking issues.\n",
